message.content:
In c:\Users\edn_y\renew_nineonelabs\resource\scss\ , I need to find cases where the SAME CSS property is declared MORE THAN ONCE inside the same rule block (not across different nested selectors). This is a bug — the first declaration gets overridden by the second silently.

Example of what to find:
```scss
.foo {
  opacity: 0;       // this is dead — overridden below
  color: red;
  opacity: 0.5;     // this wins
}
```

This is NOT a bug (different nested selectors):
```scss
.foo {
  opacity: 0;
  &:hover {
    opacity: 1;   // OK — different selector
  }
}
```

Search approach:
1. Use Grep to search each SCSS file for common properties that are most likely to be accidentally duplicated: `opacity`, `display`, `position`, `color`, `font-size`, `font-weight`, `font-family`, `line-height`, `letter-spacing`, `transform`, `transition`, `background`, `border`, `width`, `height`, `overflow`, `z-index`, `top`, `left`, `right`, `bottom`, `flex`, `gap`, `align-items`, `justify-content`, `text-align`, `cursor`, `pointer-events`, `visibility`

2. For each SCSS file in resource/scss/ (components/, layouts/, pages/, base/), look for patterns where the same property name appears twice within close proximity (within ~20 lines at the same indentation level).

3. Focus on cases where the SAME property appears at the SAME indentation level within the same block — these are definite bugs.

Report: File path, line numbers, the property name, both values (first/second), and whether it looks like a bug or not. Only report actual duplicates within the same rule block. Be thorough but focus on the files listed in git status as modified: _sub.scss, _panel.scss, _modal.scss, _drawer.scss, _footer.scss, _header.scss, _works-canvas.scss.

